<h2 id="recipe-success-tips"   class="wp-block-heading">Recipe Success Tips</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Use cold ingredients:</strong> Cold milk and cream froth up thicker and hold their shape longer. Keep them in the fridge until right before you make the foam!</li>



<li><strong>Don't over-froth:</strong> The pudding mix thickens fast, so about 10 seconds is all you need. Froth too long and it can get too thick to pour.</li>



<li><strong>Use the foam right away:</strong> Wondering how to make cold foam with pudding mix that stays fluffy? Spoon it onto your drink as soon as it's frothed, since it keeps thickening as it sits.</li>



<li><strong>Stir the syrup in first:</strong> Mix the banana bread syrup into the cold brew before adding the foam so every sip is evenly sweetened.</li>



<li><strong>Keep cold brew ready:</strong> Make a batch of cold brew and keep it in the fridge, and you can have cold brew with cold foam ready in 2 minutes any morning.</li>
</ul>



<h2 id="faqs"   class="wp-block-heading" >FAQs</h2>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1613018242329"><strong class="schema-faq-question"><strong>What is banana pudding cold foam?</strong></strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Banana pudding cold foam is a thick, creamy topping made by frothing milk and cream with instant banana pudding mix. It tastes just like classic banana pudding and sits right on top of your iced coffee or cold brew.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1791413872399"><strong class="schema-faq-question"><strong>Does Dunkin' have banana pudding cold foam?</strong></strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Dunkin' released a banana cold foam inspired by banana pudding as part of its limited-time spring banana lineup. Since it's only around for a limited time, this homemade version means you can enjoy it any time of year!</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1791413885447"><strong class="schema-faq-question"><strong>Can I make banana pudding cold foam ahead of time?</strong></strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">It's best made right before serving, since the pudding mix keeps thickening as it sits. It only takes about 10 seconds to froth, so it's easy to make fresh!</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1791413904227"><strong class="schema-faq-question"><strong>Can I make my own cold brew?</strong></strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Yes! Learning how to make banana cold brew starts with good cold brew, so steep coarsely ground coffee in cold water in the fridge for 12 to 24 hours, then strain it. Keep it in the fridge so it's ready whenever you are.</p> </div> </div>



